@startuml
' Figure 40.7  The bypassing use case
' Reading order: top to bottom. Ten loyalty calls go through the shared
' gateway, which records each in the trail. One call goes straight to
' the points server on the old ledger key. The server's own count says
' eleven; the trail says ten; conformance test K2 compares the two and
' fails, so the use case does not go live. From agentplatform.onboard
' and agentplatform.conformance.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
participant "Loyalty agent" as A <<org>>
participant "Shared gateway" as G <<ops>>
participant "Points server" as S <<ops>>
participant "Conformance" as K <<ops>>
A -> G : 10 calls
G -> S : 10 forwarded
A -[$FAIL]> S : 1 on old key
K -> S : Count: 11
K -> G : Trail: 10
K -[$FAIL]> A : K2 fails
@enduml
